From fac67eebccc3f78a3c8357bf1541200b23574594 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Scheduikat <luantak@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 08:57:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] runtime obfuscation

Allow Garble to obfuscate the runtime package without breaking the
compiler, assembler, linker, or runtime metadata contracts that refer to
runtime symbols by name.

Centralize package-path and symbol-map parsing in cmd/internal/objabi so
the compiler and linker use one translation model. Apply that model to
compiler intrinsics, runtime builtins, ABI identities, reflection data,
pclntab generation, and linker symbol resolution. Preserve the narrow
assembly and platform contracts that cannot be renamed.

Keep tiny and reverse modes symmetric by carrying the custom pclntab
magic and entry-offset key through the linker. Add focused tests for map
parsing, missing builtins, runtime function identities, and metadata
translation.

Refs https://github.com/burrowers/garble/issues/193
